{
  "_readme": [
    "THIS IS THE ONLY FILE YOU NEED TO EDIT.",
    "",
    "To add a guest      -> add an object to a party's `members` array.",
    "To remove a guest   -> delete that object.",
    "To add a new family -> add a new object to `parties` with a unique `party_id`.",
    "",
    "Then run:  npm run generate-invites   (or just push - the build does it automatically)",
    "",
    "RULES:",
    "  * `party_id` must be unique and must NEVER be changed once links are sent,",
    "     because the slug is derived from it. Changing it changes that family's link.",
    "  * `english_name` must NEVER be changed once links are sent, for the same reason.",
    "  * `farsi_name` CAN be edited freely at any time - it does not affect the link.",
    "  * Set `english_name` to null for a person whose name you don't know yet.",
    "     They still get a working link, flagged as NEEDS-NAME in links-export.csv.",
    "  * Exactly one member per party should have \"is_head\": true.",
    "",
    "Adding/removing guests NEVER changes anybody else's existing link."
  ],

